  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_intro",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Lorenz Attractor — Deterministic Chaos 🦋\n\nIn 1963, meteorologist **Edward Lorenz** discovered that a simple system of three coupled differential equations could produce wildly unpredictable, non-repeating motion. This was the birth of **chaos theory** and the famous **butterfly effect**.\n\n## The Lorenz System\n\nThe three equations describe convective fluid motion:\n\n$$\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\sigma(y - x)$$\n\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt} = x(\\rho - z) - y$$\n\n$$\\frac{dz}{dt} = xy - \\beta z$$\n\nwhere:\n- $\\sigma$ (sigma) — Prandtl number, ratio of momentum diffusivity to thermal diffusivity\n- $\\rho$ (rho) — Rayleigh number ratio, related to the temperature difference driving convection\n- $\\beta$ (beta) — geometric factor\n\n## The Butterfly Attractor\n\nWith the classic parameters $\\sigma = 10$, $\\rho = 28$, $\\beta = 8/3 \\approx 2.667$, the system never settles — the trajectory orbits two lobes forever, tracing the iconic **butterfly-shaped strange attractor**.\n\n**Sensitivity to initial conditions**: Two trajectories starting $10^{-10}$ apart will diverge exponentially. This is the mathematical heart of the butterfly effect — a butterfly flapping its wings in Brazil could (in principle) set off a tornado in Texas.\n\n## This Notebook\n\n- **Cell 2** — interactive sliders to tune $\\sigma$, $\\rho$, $\\beta$ in real time\n- **Cell 3** — live 60 FPS simulation with RK4 integration and spectral trail rendering\n- **Cell 4** — real-time dashboard showing current position and parameters",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_params",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Parameters",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "(\n    ui::slider(\"sigma\", 1.0, 30.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"\\u{03c3} (Sigma)\")\n        .default_value(10.0),\n    ui::slider(\"rho\", 1.0, 50.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"\\u{03c1} (Rho)\")\n        .default_value(28.0),\n    ui::slider(\"beta\", 0.1, 10.0)\n        .step(0.01)\n        .label(\"\\u{03b2} (Beta)\")\n        .default_value(2.667),\n)",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_sim",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Lorenz Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Lorenz Attractor — live Simulation trait implementation.\n//\n// RK4 integration of the Lorenz system with sub-steps for accuracy.\n// Trail is rendered into a pixel buffer using additive blending and\n// a spectral color gradient keyed on the z-value.\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 600;\nconst TRAIL_LEN: usize = 3000;\nconst SUB_STEPS: u32 = 10;\nconst DT: f64 = 0.005;\n\n// ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstruct LorenzSim {\n    x: f64,\n    y: f64,\n    z: f64,\n    trail: Vec<(f64, f64, f64)>,\n}\n\n// ── Color helper ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/// Map z ∈ [0, 50] to a spectral RGB color scaled by brightness ∈ [0, 255].\nfn z_color(z: f64, brightness: u8) -> (u8, u8, u8) {\n    let t = (z / 50.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n    let b = brightness as f64 / 255.0;\n    let (r, g, bl) = if t < 0.25 {\n        let s = t / 0.25;\n        (0.0_f64, s, 1.0_f64)\n    } else if t < 0.5 {\n        let s = (t - 0.25) / 0.25;\n        (0.0, 1.0, 1.0 - s)\n    } else if t < 0.75 {\n        let s = (t - 0.5) / 0.25;\n        (s, 1.0, 0.0)\n    } else {\n        let s = (t - 0.75) / 0.25;\n        (1.0, 1.0 - s, 0.0)\n    };\n    (\n        (r * b * 255.0) as u8,\n        (g * b * 255.0) as u8,\n        (bl * b * 255.0) as u8,\n    )\n}\n\n// ── Simulation trait ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimpl Simulation for LorenzSim {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            x: 1.0,\n            y: 1.0,\n            z: 1.0,\n            trail: Vec::with_capacity(TRAIL_LEN),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        let sigma = sim::read::<f64>(\"sigma\").unwrap_or(10.0);\n        let rho   = sim::read::<f64>(\"rho\").unwrap_or(28.0);\n        let beta  = sim::read::<f64>(\"beta\").unwrap_or(2.667);\n\n        // RK4 with sub-steps for numerical stability.\n        for _ in 0..SUB_STEPS {\n            let (x, y, z) = (self.x, self.y, self.z);\n\n            let k1x = sigma * (y - x);\n            let k1y = x * (rho - z) - y;\n            let k1z = x * y - beta * z;\n\n            let x2 = x + DT / 2.0 * k1x;\n            let y2 = y + DT / 2.0 * k1y;\n            let z2 = z + DT / 2.0 * k1z;\n            let k2x = sigma * (y2 - x2);\n            let k2y = x2 * (rho - z2) - y2;\n            let k2z = x2 * y2 - beta * z2;\n\n            let x3 = x + DT / 2.0 * k2x;\n            let y3 = y + DT / 2.0 * k2y;\n            let z3 = z + DT / 2.0 * k2z;\n            let k3x = sigma * (y3 - x3);\n            let k3y = x3 * (rho - z3) - y3;\n            let k3z = x3 * y3 - beta * z3;\n\n            let x4 = x + DT * k3x;\n            let y4 = y + DT * k3y;\n            let z4 = z + DT * k3z;\n            let k4x = sigma * (y4 - x4);\n            let k4y = x4 * (rho - z4) - y4;\n            let k4z = x4 * y4 - beta * z4;\n\n            self.x += DT / 6.0 * (k1x + 2.0 * k2x + 2.0 * k3x + k4x);\n            self.y += DT / 6.0 * (k1y + 2.0 * k2y + 2.0 * k3y + k4y);\n            self.z += DT / 6.0 * (k1z + 2.0 * k2z + 2.0 * k3z + k4z);\n        }\n\n        // Append current position to trail.\n        self.trail.push((self.x, self.y, self.z));\n        if self.trail.len() > TRAIL_LEN {\n            self.trail.remove(0);\n        }\n\n        // Publish telemetry for the dashboard and instruments cells.\n        sim::emit(\"x\", &self.x);\n        sim::emit(\"y\", &self.y);\n        sim::emit(\"z\", &self.z);\n        sim::emit(\"trail_len\", &(self.trail.len() as u64));\n\n        // ── Render ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        // Pre-render the trail into a pixel buffer using additive blending,\n        // then hand the buffer to Canvas::from_fn for zero-copy upload.\n        //\n        // Projection: XZ plane (shows the classic butterfly best).\n        //   x ∈ [-25, 25]  →  [0, W]\n        //   z ∈ [  0, 55]  →  [H, 0]  (z grows upward)\n\n        let mut buf = vec![(8u8, 8u8, 15u8); (W * H) as usize];\n        let trail_len = self.trail.len();\n\n        for (i, &(tx, ty_unused, tz)) in self.trail.iter().enumerate() {\n            let _ = ty_unused;\n            let age = i as f64 / trail_len as f64; // 0 = oldest, 1 = newest\n            let brightness = (40.0 + 215.0 * age) as u8;\n            let (cr, cg, cb) = z_color(tz, brightness);\n\n            let sx = ((tx + 25.0) / 50.0 * W as f64) as i32;\n            let sy = (H as f64 - tz / 55.0 * H as f64) as i32;\n\n            for dy in -1_i32..=1 {\n                for dx in -1_i32..=1 {\n                    let px = sx + dx;\n                    let py = sy + dy;\n                    if px >= 0 && px < W as i32 && py >= 0 && py < H as i32 {\n                        let idx = (py as u32 * W + px as u32) as usize;\n                        buf[idx].0 = buf[idx].0.saturating_add(cr / 3);\n                        buf[idx].1 = buf[idx].1.saturating_add(cg / 3);\n                        buf[idx].2 = buf[idx].2.saturating_add(cb / 3);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Highlight the current point with a bright white glow.\n        let head_sx = ((self.x + 25.0) / 50.0 * W as f64) as i32;\n        let head_sy = (H as f64 - self.z / 55.0 * H as f64) as i32;\n        for dy in -3_i32..=3 {\n            for dx in -3_i32..=3 {\n                if dx * dx + dy * dy <= 9 {\n                    let px = head_sx + dx;\n                    let py = head_sy + dy;\n                    if px >= 0 && px < W as i32 && py >= 0 && py < H as i32 {\n                        let idx = (py as u32 * W + px as u32) as usize;\n                        buf[idx] = (255, 255, 255);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        Canvas::from_fn(W, H, |px, py| {\n            buf[(py * W + px) as usize]\n        })\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        60\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_dashboard",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Dashboard",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "/// # Lorenz Attractor Dashboard — LiveView\n///\n/// Reads telemetry published by the simulation cell and renders\n/// a real-time status panel.\n\nstruct Dashboard {\n    tick: u32,\n}\n\nimpl LiveView for Dashboard {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { tick: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        self.tick += 1;\n\n        let x     = sim::read::<f64>(\"x\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let y     = sim::read::<f64>(\"y\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let z     = sim::read::<f64>(\"z\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let sigma = sim::read::<f64>(\"sigma\").unwrap_or(10.0);\n        let rho   = sim::read::<f64>(\"rho\").unwrap_or(28.0);\n        let beta  = sim::read::<f64>(\"beta\").unwrap_or(2.667);\n        let trail = sim::read::<u64>(\"trail_len\").unwrap_or(0);\n\n        LiveContent::Html(format!(r#\"<div style=\"font-family: monospace; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a0a1a, #1a1a3e); color: #e0e0e0; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #2a2a5a;\">\n  <div style=\"color: #7070cc; font-size: 0.75em; letter-spacing: 0.15em; margin-bottom: 12px;\">LORENZ ATTRACTOR — LIVE TELEMETRY</div>\n  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n    <div>\n      <div style=\"color: #555; font-size: 0.75em; margin-bottom: 4px;\">POSITION</div>\n      <div>x = <span style=\"color: #ff6b6b;\">{x:+.4}</span></div>\n      <div>y = <span style=\"color: #4fc3f7;\">{y:+.4}</span></div>\n      <div>z = <span style=\"color: #69f0ae;\">{z:+.4}</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <div style=\"color: #555; font-size: 0.75em; margin-bottom: 4px;\">PARAMETERS</div>\n      <div>σ = <span style=\"color: #ffcc80;\">{sigma:.1}</span></div>\n      <div>ρ = <span style=\"color: #ffcc80;\">{rho:.1}</span></div>\n      <div>β = <span style=\"color: #ffcc80;\">{beta:.3}</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <div style=\"color: #555; font-size: 0.75em; margin-bottom: 4px;\">TRAIL</div>\n      <div><span style=\"color: #ce93d8;\">{trail}</span> points</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\"#))\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        10\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    }
  ]
}